        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: शाकम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शाकम् (śākam) — \"a vegetable, a green\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शाकम् (śākam) is a vegetable, and especially a leaf one — the cooked greens that a Hindi menu calls साग."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Where पत्रम् is the leaf on a लता, शाकम् (śākam) is the leaf in a pot."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "MW calls its derivation doubtful. The word stayed home, and it is doing the same work today it was doing three thousand years ago."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Śāka is of doubtful derivation, MW says. It lives on as Prakrit sāga (CDIAL 12370); Hindi and Punjabi sāg look like its descendants, though CDIAL does not list them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Leaves on the plant, and leaves in the pot."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
